    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it doesn't feel temporary. it feels like he actually took me with him. like the person who knew how to live, how to laugh, how to exist... that person is just dead. i'm just the leftovers. i move around, i eat, i sleep, but there's nobody actually home. it's just this heavy, hollow nothingness.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
